  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training Logistics &amp; Planning and Intermodal Transport</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Given various developments in the maritime sector on a national and regional scale, the Comision Portuaria Nacional Guatemala faces significant challenges for development. Understanding international standards and best practices is crucial to deal with these challenges.A similar programme has been successfully executed in 2015 in Nicaragua, with the support of Nuffic. Participants were 23 managers from the Empresa Portuaria Nacional Nicaragua and five from Guatemala.The goal is to improve efficiency in Guatemalan ports and logistics sector. The project will contribute by training 25 managers from different ports on Logistics &amp; Planning and Intermodal Transport to further disseminate knowledge on international best practices in the Guatemalan port sector.Training will, most likely, will be provided in Guatemala to managers from Guatemalan ports on both coasts of the country.</narrative>
  </description>
